\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {8.2}{\ignorespaces Wall time at the pattern and scale of \citet  {sulzmannlu2014}'s Figure~7. \texttt  {deriv\_bc} is directly comparable to \texttt  {parseBC} (their Figures~5 and~6); the narrower \texttt  {DERIV} implementation the paper actually plots solves an easier, submatching-only problem, and \texttt  {pderiv\_bc}/ \texttt  {pderiv\_std} are this project's own partial-derivative constructions, not benchmarked by either paper. Wall time is the match-side entry's own reported \texttt  {micros}; the non-match side is within a few percent throughout and omitted. \texttt  {deriv\_std\_rec} and \texttt  {deriv\_std\_loop} crash at every point tested on both rows, the same input lengths that Table~\ref {tab:patho-crash-thresholds} locates precisely for every representative row.}}{73}{figure.caption.53}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:patho-fig7}{{8.2}{73}{Wall time at the pattern and scale of \citet {sulzmannlu2014}'s Figure~7. \texttt {deriv\_bc} is directly comparable to \texttt {parseBC} (their Figures~5 and~6); the narrower \texttt {DERIV} implementation the paper actually plots solves an easier, submatching-only problem, and \texttt {pderiv\_bc}/ \texttt {pderiv\_std} are this project's own partial-derivative constructions, not benchmarked by either paper. Wall time is the match-side entry's own reported \texttt {micros}; the non-match side is within a few percent throughout and omitted. \texttt {deriv\_std\_rec} and \texttt {deriv\_std\_loop} crash at every point tested on both rows, the same input lengths that Table~\ref {tab:patho-crash-thresholds} locates precisely for every representative row}{figure.caption.53}{}}
